        "selections": {
          "{\"uri\":\"file:///c%3A/Users/pc/.cursor/plans/pcb_ledger_complete_history_system_with_api_implementation_6e5d61a4.plan.md\",\"range\":{\"selectionStartLineNumber\":1,\"selectionStartColumn\":1,\"positionLineNumber\":410,\"positionColumn\":1},\"text\":\"# PCB Ledger Complete History System with API Implementation\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nTransform PCB Ledger from event-based entries to a \\\"one file per PCB\\\" system that stores complete history with master snapshots at every event. Includes sophisticated API system with centralized ground rules, robust error handling, and comprehensive debug logging.\\n\\n## Architecture\\n\\n### Current State\\n\\n- **PCB Ledger**: One document per event (many documents per PCB)\\n- **PCB Master**: Current state only (no history)\\n\\n### Target State\\n\\n- **PCB Ledger**: One document per PCB serial (contains timeline child table)\\n- **PCB Ledger Timeline**: Child table with append-only events\\n- **Centralized Ground Rules**: All API formats defined in one place ([PCB_LEDGER_GROUND_RULES.md](PCB_LEDGER_GROUND_RULES.md))\\n- **Sophisticated API**: Never breaks main document flow, extensible payload structure\\n\\n## Data Model Design\\n\\n### 1. PCB Ledger DocType (One per PCB Serial)\\n\\n#### Identity Fields\\n\\n- `name`: PCB Serial Number (Primary Key, e.g., \\\"SLC001\\\")\\n- `pcb_serial_no`: Data (Required)\\n- `item_code`: Link → Item\\n- `pcb_revision`, `batch_no`, `manufacturing_lot`: Optional\\n\\n#### Lifecycle Tracking\\n\\n- `lifecycle_stage`: Select (INBOUND → INCOMING_QC → PTS_TESTING → STORES → ASSEMBLY → REJECTED → SCRAP)\\n- `first_received_on`, `first_tested_on`, `last_event_time`: Datetime\\n- `last_known_location`: Link → Warehouse\\n- `total_test_count`, `total_rework_count`: Int\\n\\n#### Current Snapshot (Mirrors PCB Master)\\n\\n- `overall_status`, `current_warehouse`, `pts1_status`, `pts2_status`, `pts3_status`\\n- `dominant_channel`, `max_value`, `remark`, `iqc_date`, `last_tested_on`\\n- `last_event_ref_doctype`, `last_event_ref_docname`\\n\\n### 2. PCB Ledger Timeline (Child Table)\\n\\n#### Event Fields\\n\\n- `event_time`: Datetime (Required)\\n- `event_type`: Select (Required)\\n- `stage_after_event`: Select\\n- `actor_user`: Link → User\\n- `from_location`, `to_location`: Link → Warehouse\\n- `ref_doctype`, `ref_docname`: Data\\n- `remarks`: Small Text\\n\\n#### Snapshot Fields\\n\\n- `master_snapshot_json`: Long Text (JSON) - Complete structured snapshot\\n- `extra_payload_json`: Long Text (JSON) - Event-specific data\\n\\n## Ground Rules Configuration\\n\\n**File**: [PCB_LEDGER_GROUND_RULES.md](PCB_LEDGER_GROUND_RULES.md)\\n\\nCentralized configuration defining:\\n\\n- Event type mapping for each DocType\\n- Payload structure for each source\\n- PCB serial extraction methods\\n- Lifecycle stage mapping\\n\\n**Key Principle**: Change API format once in ground rules → all integrations update automatically\\n\\n### Ground Rules Structure\\n\\n1. **Purchase Receipt Rule**\\n\\n   - Event Type: `RECEIVED_IN_OFFICE`\\n   - Lifecycle Stage: `INBOUND`\\n   - PCB Serial Extraction: From `items[].serial_no` field\\n   - Payload Builder: `build_purchase_receipt_payload()`\\n\\n2. **Stock Entry Rules** (Multiple types)\\n\\n   - `PCB-IQC-Accept` → `MOVED_TO_STORES` (STORES)\\n   - `PCB-IQC-Reject` → `MOVED_TO_REJECTED` (REJECTED)\\n   - `Transfereing PCB to PTS testing` → `MOVED_TO_PTS_TESTING` (PTS_TESTING)\\n   - `Material Transfer for Manufacture` → `MOVED_TO_ASSEMBLY` (ASSEMBLY)\\n   - `Rejected from Assembly` → `MOVED_TO_REJECTED` (REJECTED)\\n   - PCB Serial Extraction: From `custom_pcb[]` table\\n   - Payload Builder: `build_stock_entry_payload()` (includes operator / station metadata for PTS transfers and supports deriving PTS dwell-time metrics in the ledger snapshot)\\n\\n3. **PCB IQC Result Rule**\\n\\n   - Primary Event Type: `IQC_RESULT_RECORDED` (one event per IQC submission and PCB serial, includes `attempt_no` and optional `failure_codes` where available)\\n   - Optional fine-grained events (for future/advanced analytics): `PTS1_UPDATED`, `PTS2_UPDATED`, `PTS3_UPDATED`, `IQC_SUBMITTED`\\n   - Lifecycle Stage: `PTS_TESTING`\\n   - PCB Serial Extraction: From `table_jqbb[]` (or PCB IQC Line table)\\n   - Payload Builder: `build_pcb_iqc_result_payload()` (responsible for populating `event_data` with IQC statuses, attempt number and failure codes)\\n\\n4. **PCB Master Rule**\\n\\n   - Event Type: `STATUS_COMPUTED`\\n   - Lifecycle Stage: Auto-detect from `overall_status`\\n   - PCB Serial Extraction: Document name = serial number\\n   - Payload Builder: `build_pcb_master_payload()`\\n\\n## API Module Implementation\\n\\n**File**: `erpnext/stock/doctype/pcb_ledger/pcb_ledger_api.py`\\n\\n### Main Function: `update_pcb_ledger()`\\n\\n```python\\n@frappe.whitelist()\\ndef update_pcb_ledger(event_payload):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Sophisticated API - Never breaks, only returns error responses\\n    \\n    Args:\\n        event_payload (dict): Structured payload from ground rules\\n    \\n    Returns:\\n        dict: {\\n            \\\"success\\\": bool,\\n            \\\"ledger_docname\\\": str,\\n            \\\"timeline_entry_created\\\": bool,\\n            \\\"event_id\\\": str,\\n            \\\"error\\\": dict (if failed)\\n        }\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n```\\n\\n**Features**:\\n\\n- Input validation (structured errors)\\n- Never raises exceptions (always returns response)\\n- Comprehensive logging (F12 console + server logs)\\n- Extensible payload structure\\n- Idempotent (safe to retry)\\n\\n### Helper Functions\\n\\n- `validate_pcb_ledger_input()`: Validates payload structure\\n- `get_or_create_pcb_ledger()`: Safely gets or creates ledger document\\n- `build_master_snapshot()`: Builds complete structured snapshot from PCB Master\\n- `append_timeline_entry()`: Appends timeline entry with validation\\n- `update_ledger_snapshot()`: Updates current snapshot fields\\n- `handle_api_error()`: Standardized error response formatter\\n\\n### Event Payload Structure (Extensible)\\n\\n```python\\n{\\n    \\\"api_version\\\": \\\"1.0\\\",\\n    \\\"event_type\\\": \\\"MOVED_TO_STORES\\\",\\n    \\\"event_timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-02-01 10:00:00\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": {\\n        \\\"doctype\\\": \\\"Stock Entry\\\",\\n        \\\"docname\\\": \\\"STE-00045\\\",\\n        \\\"user\\\": \\\"operator@company.com\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"pcb_data\\\": {\\n        \\\"pcb_serial_no\\\": \\\"SLC001\\\",  # Required\\n        \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"PA01 0001\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"event_data\\\": {\\n        # Event-specific data (extensible)\\n    },\\n    \\\"location_data\\\": {\\n        \\\"from_location\\\": \\\"PTS Testing - R\\\",\\n        \\\"to_location\\\": \\\"Stores - R\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n        # Additional metadata (extensible)\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Integration Points\\n\\n### 1. Purchase Receipt Integration\\n\\n**File**: Server Script on `Purchase Receipt` → `on_submit`\\n\\n**Pattern**:\\n\\n1. Get ground rule: `get_ledger_rule(\\\"Purchase Receipt\\\")`\\n2. Extract PCB serials: `extract_pcb_serials_from_purchase_receipt(doc, rule)`\\n3. Build payload: `build_purchase_receipt_payload(doc, item, pcb_serial_no)`\\n4. Call API: `update_pcb_ledger(event_payload)`\\n5. Handle result: Log errors, don't break flow\\n\\n**Event Type**: `RECEIVED_IN_OFFICE`\\n\\n**Lifecycle Stage**: `INBOUND`\\n\\n### 2. Stock Entry Integration\\n\\n**File**: Server Script on `Stock Entry` → `on_submit`\\n\\n**Pattern**:\\n\\n1. Get ground rule: `get_ledger_rule(\\\"Stock Entry\\\", doc.stock_entry_type)`\\n2. Extract PCB serials: `extract_pcb_serials_from_stock_entry(doc, rule)`\\n3. Build payload: `build_stock_entry_payload(doc, pcb_row, event_type, from_warehouse, to_warehouse)`\\n4. Call API: `update_pcb_ledger(event_payload)`\\n5. Handle result: Process each PCB individually, log errors\\n\\n**Stock Entry Types & Event Mappings**:\\n\\n- `PCB-IQC-Accept` → `MOVED_TO_STORES` (STORES)\\n- `PCB-IQC-Reject` → `MOVED_TO_REJECTED` (REJECTED)\\n- `Transfereing PCB to PTS testing` → `MOVED_TO_PTS_TESTING` (PTS_TESTING)\\n- `Material Transfer for Manufacture` → `MOVED_TO_ASSEMBLY` (ASSEMBLY)\\n- `Rejected from Assembly` → `MOVED_TO_REJECTED` (REJECTED)\\n\\n### 3. PCB IQC Result Integration\\n\\n**File**: Modify `pcb_iqc_result_api.py`\\n\\n**Pattern**:\\n\\n1. Get ground rule: `get_ledger_rule(\\\"PCB IQC Result\\\")`\\n2. Determine event type: `determine_iqc_event_type(pcb_row, rule)`\\n3. Build payload: `build_pcb_iqc_result_payload(doc, pcb_row, event_type)`\\n4. Call API: `update_pcb_ledger(event_payload)`\\n5. Handle result: Log errors, don't break main flow\\n\\n**Event Types**:\\n\\n- `PTS1_UPDATED`: When PTS1 status is set\\n- `PTS2_UPDATED`: When PTS2 status is set\\n- `PTS3_UPDATED`: When PTS3 status is set\\n- `IQC_SUBMITTED`: When document is submitted\\n\\n**Lifecycle Stage**: `PTS_TESTING`\\n\\n### 4. PCB Master Integration\\n\\n**File**: Server Script on `PCB Master` → `on_update`\\n\\n**Pattern**:\\n\\n1. Get ground rule: `get_ledger_rule(\\\"PCB Master\\\")`\\n2. Check changed fields: `get_changed_fields(doc)`\\n3. Build payload: `build_pcb_master_payload(doc, changed_fields)`\\n4. Call API: `update_pcb_ledger(event_payload)`\\n5. Handle result: Log errors\\n\\n**Event Type**: `STATUS_COMPUTED`\\n\\n**Lifecycle Stage**: Auto-detect from `overall_status`\\n\\n## Debug Logging Strategy\\n\\n### 1. F12 Console Logging (Client-Side)\\n\\n**In Client Scripts**:\\n\\n```javascript\\nconsole.log('[PCB Ledger API]', {\\n    action: 'Calling API',\\n    doctype: 'Stock Entry',\\n    docname: frm.doc.name,\\n    payload: event_payload\\n});\\n\\nfrappe.call({\\n    method: 'erpnext.stock.doctype.pcb_ledger.pcb_ledger_api.update_pcb_ledger',\\n    args: { event_payload: event_payload },\\n    callback: function(r) {\\n        console.log('[PCB Ledger API] Response:', r);\\n        if (!r.message || !r.message.success) {\\n            console.error('[PCB Ledger API] Error:', r.message);\\n        }\\n    },\\n    error: function(r) {\\n        console.error('[PCB Ledger API] Request Failed:', r);\\n    }\\n});\\n```\\n\\n### 2. Server-Side Logging\\n\\n**In API Module**:\\n\\n- Log input payload\\n- Log validation errors\\n- Log processing steps\\n- Log success/failure\\n- Log exceptions with traceback\\n\\n**In Server Scripts**:\\n\\n- Log when integration starts\\n- Log payload being sent\\n- Log API response\\n- Log errors (don't break flow)\\n\\n## Error Handling Strategy\\n\\n### Never Break Main Flow\\n\\nAll integrations use try-catch blocks and handle errors gracefully:\\n\\n- Log errors to server logs\\n- Optionally show non-blocking warnings to users\\n- Never raise exceptions that break main document flow\\n- Process each PCB individually (one failure doesn't stop others)\\n\\n### Structured Error Responses\\n\\n```python\\n{\\n    \\\"success\\\": False,\\n    \\\"error_code\\\": \\\"VALIDATION_ERROR\\\",\\n    \\\"error_message\\\": \\\"PCB serial number is required\\\",\\n    \\\"field\\\": \\\"pcb_data.pcb_serial_no\\\",\\n    \\\"details\\\": {\\n        \\\"provided\\\": None,\\n        \\\"expected\\\": \\\"string (non-empty)\\\"\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Visual Timeline Display\\n\\n**File**: Client Script for PCB Ledger DocType\\n\\n**Two Display Formats** (using same data):\\n\\n1. **Vertical Timeline**: Events stacked vertically with markers and connecting lines\\n2. **Table Format**: Sortable, filterable table with all columns\\n\\n**Features**:\\n\\n- Toggle button to switch between views\\n- Click marker/row to see full snapshot JSON\\n- Print-friendly CSS\\n- Mobile-responsive\\n\\n## Implementation Steps\\n\\n### Phase 1: Restructure PCB Ledger DocType\\n\\n1. Create new PCB Ledger structure (one doc per PCB serial)\\n2. Create PCB Ledger Timeline child table DocType\\n\\n### Phase 2: Create Ground Rules Configuration\\n\\n1. Create [PCB_LEDGER_GROUND_RULES.md](PCB_LEDGER_GROUND_RULES.md)\\n2. Define rules for all 4 DocTypes\\n3. Create payload builder functions\\n\\n### Phase 3: Create API Module\\n\\n1. Create `pcb_ledger_api.py`\\n2. Implement `update_pcb_ledger()` with validation\\n3. Implement helper functions\\n4. Add comprehensive logging\\n\\n### Phase 4: Integrate Each DocType\\n\\n1. **Purchase Receipt**: Create server script `on_submit` using ground rules\\n2. **Stock Entry**: Create/modify server script `on_submit` using ground rules\\n3. **PCB IQC Result**: Modify `pcb_iqc_result_api.py` using ground rules\\n4. **PCB Master**: Create server script `on_update` using ground rules\\n\\n### Phase 5: Add Debug Logging\\n\\n1. Add F12 console logging in client scripts\\n2. Add server-side logging in API module\\n3. Add logging in all server scripts\\n\\n### Phase 6: Create Visual Timeline Display\\n\\n1. Create client script for PCB Ledger DocType\\n2. Implement Vertical Timeline view\\n3. Implement Table Format view\\n4. Add toggle functionality\\n\\n### Phase 7: Testing & Validation\\n\\n1. Test each integration point\\n2. Verify error handling\\n3. Check debug logs (F12 + server)\\n4. Verify extensibility (add new fields)\\n5. Test complete workflow end-to-end\\n\\n## Key Principles\\n\\n1. **Ground Rules First**: All API formats defined in centralized config\\n2. **Never Break**: API errors don't break main document flow\\n3. **Extensible**: Add fields without breaking existing code\\n4. **Debuggable**: Comprehensive logging everywhere (F12 + server)\\n5. **Consistent**: Same pattern across all integrations\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n- API works from all 4 DocTypes\\n- Ground rules centralized (change once, applies everywhere)\\n- Debug statements in F12 console\\n- Server-side logging for all operations\\n- Error handling never breaks main flow\\n- Extensible payload structure\\n- Clear error messages\\n- Visual timeline display working\\n- Complete workflow tested end-to-end\"}": []
        },
